// ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓
// ┃          Niri Configuration (mirrored from Hyprland)        ┃
// ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛

// ======= Input =======
input {
    keyboard {
	    repeat-rate 35
	    repeat-delay 250

        xkb {
        }
    }

    mouse {
        // off disables all acceleration
        // accel-speed 0.0
    }

    // Follow mouse focus (like Hyprland follow_mouse = 2)
    focus-follows-mouse max-scroll-amount="0%"
    warp-mouse-to-focus
}

// ======= Outputs (Monitors) =======
// DELIBERATELY EMPTY. niri enables every connected output at its preferred
// mode by default, which is the portable behaviour we want across every host.
// Adding output blocks here is what BREAKS portability -- they are appended
// per machine by modules/hosts/<host>.nix via `my.niri.extra`.
// Do not add kanshi: it races with niri (niri-wm/niri#676).

// ======= Layout =======
layout {
    // gaps = space between windows (like Hyprland gaps_in)
    gaps 5

    center-focused-column "never"

    preset-column-widths {
        proportion 0.33333
        proportion 0.5
        proportion 0.66667
    }

    default-column-width {
        proportion 0.5
    }

    focus-ring {
        off
    }

    border {
        width 3
        active-color "#8b3d3d"
        inactive-color "#4a2222"
    }

    // Struts = outer gaps (like Hyprland gaps_out)
    struts {
        left 5
        right 5
        top 5
        bottom 5
    }
}

// ======= Visual / Decorations =======
prefer-no-csd

// ======= Animations =======
animations {
    // niri has smooth defaults; customize if desired
    // slowdown 1.0
}

// ======= Window Rules =======
// Float equivalent windows (niri uses open-floating)
window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^blueman-manager$"#
    open-floating true
}
window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^xdg-desktop-portal"#
    open-floating true
}
window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^polkit-"#
    open-floating true
}
window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^org\.kde\.polkit"#
    open-floating true
}
window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^zenity$"#
    open-floating true
}
window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^gnome-calculator$"#
    open-floating true
}
window-rule {
    match title="Picture-in-Picture"
    open-floating true
}
window-rule {
    match title="Picture in picture"
    open-floating true
}
window-rule {
    match title="Save File"
    open-floating true
}
window-rule {
    match title="Open File"
    open-floating true
}

// Opacity rules
window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^(thunar|nemo)$"#
    opacity 0.97
}
window-rule {
    match app-id=r#"^(discord|armcord|webcord)$"#
    opacity 0.96
}

// Wiremix: tiled, quarter-width
window-rule {
    match title="wiremix"
    default-column-width { proportion 0.25; }
}

// Corner radius for all windows
window-rule {
    geometry-corner-radius 4 4 4 4
    clip-to-geometry true
}

// ======= Cursor =======
cursor {
    xcursor-theme "vimix-kanagawa-cursors-lotus"
    xcursor-size 16
}

// ======= Environment =======
environment {
    // xwayland-satellite runs on :1 — SDDM's Xorg greeter owns :0.
    // Pointing at :0 gets "Authorization required" (root-owned, its own xauth).
    DISPLAY ":1"
    QT_CURSOR_SIZE "16"
    XCURSOR_THEME "vimix-kanagawa-cursors-lotus"
    XCURSOR_SIZE "16"
}

// ======= Autostart =======
spawn-at-startup "xwayland-satellite" ":1"
spawn-at-startup "swaybg" "-o" "*" "-i" "@WALLPAPER@" "-m" "stretch"
// waybar is NOT spawned here. It is a systemd user unit — see
// modules/desktop/waybar.nix. The compositor is still bringing outputs up when
// the session target is reached and waybar dies on that race; `Restart=always`
// is the cure, and spawn-at-startup cannot restart anything. Starting it in
// BOTH places yields two bars.
spawn-at-startup "fcitx5" "-d"
spawn-at-startup "mako"
// nm-applet removed — using iwd/iwctl via custom waybar module instead
spawn-at-startup "/usr/lib/polkit-kde-authentication-agent-1"
spawn-at-startup "swayidle" "-w" "timeout" "300" "swaylock -f -c 000000" "before-sleep" "swaylock -f -c 000000"

// systemd/dbus integration
spawn-at-startup "sh" "-c" "systemctl --user import-environment && dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd WAYLAND_DISPLAY XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=niri"

// ======= Key Bindings =======
binds {
    // ─── Escape a keyboard-grabbing window (RDP / Chromium keyboard lock) ───
    //
    // niri's own action, called directly. This used to route through
    // scripts/kbd-inhibit.sh, which also kept a per-window ledger to drive a
    // waybar indicator; the ledger could only ever guess, so both were removed
    // on 2026-08-21. `git log -- config/niri/scripts/kbd-inhibit.sh` has the
    // full reasoning.
    //
    // allow-inhibiting=false is what makes this bind the escape hatch: it is
    // the one key niri refuses to hand to an inhibiting client, so it still
    // arrives when a window has grabbed everything else.
    Mod+Escape allow-inhibiting=false { toggle-keyboard-shortcuts-inhibit; }

    // ─── Launch Programs ───
    Mod+Return { spawn "alacritty"; }
    Mod+E      { spawn "nemo"; }
    Mod+Space  { spawn "rofi" "-show" "combi" "-modi" "window,run,combi" "-combi-modi" "window,run"; }
    Mod+A      { spawn "sh" "-c" "grim -g \"$(slurp)\" - | swappy -f -"; }
    Mod+W      { spawn "gnome-calculator"; }
    Mod+M      { spawn "sh" "-c" "wl-paste > /tmp/clipboard.md && bunx markdown-to-html-cli -s /tmp/clipboard.md -o /tmp/clipboard.html --no-dark-mode && zen-browser /tmp/clipboard.html"; }
    Mod+G      { power-off-monitors; }
    Mod+O      { toggle-overview; }
    Mod+Shift+Grave { spawn "alacritty" "--title" "wiremix" "-e" "wiremix"; }
    Mod+Shift+O { spawn "systemctl" "--user" "restart" "waybar"; }

    // ─── Window Actions ───
    Mod+Q           { close-window; }
    Mod+Shift+M     { quit skip-confirmation=true; }
    Mod+F           { maximize-column; }
    Mod+Shift+F     { fullscreen-window; }
    Mod+V           { toggle-window-floating; }

    // ─── Focus (vim keys + arrows) ───
    // H/L navigate between columns on the horizontal strip
    Mod+H     { focus-column-left; }
    Mod+L     { focus-column-right; }
    // J/K navigate windows in column, then workspaces
    Mod+J     { focus-window-or-workspace-down; }
    Mod+K     { focus-window-or-workspace-up; }
    // N/P toggle between monitors (vertically stacked)
    Mod+N     { focus-monitor-down; }
    Mod+P     { focus-monitor-up; }
    Mod+Left  { focus-column-left; }
    Mod+Right { focus-column-right; }
    Mod+Down  { focus-window-or-workspace-down; }
    Mod+Up    { focus-window-or-workspace-up; }

    // ─── Move Windows (niri way: consume/expel on H/L, workspace on J/K) ───
    Mod+Shift+H     { spawn "sh" "-c" "niri msg action reset-window-height; niri msg action consume-or-expel-window-left"; }
    Mod+Shift+L     { spawn "sh" "-c" "niri msg action reset-window-height; niri msg action consume-or-expel-window-right"; }
    Mod+Shift+J     { move-window-down-or-to-workspace-down; }
    Mod+Shift+K     { move-window-up-or-to-workspace-up; }
    // Shift+N/P: move window to other monitor
    Mod+Shift+N     { move-column-to-monitor-down; }
    Mod+Shift+P     { move-column-to-monitor-up; }
    Mod+Shift+Left  { spawn "sh" "-c" "niri msg action reset-window-height; niri msg action consume-or-expel-window-left"; }
    Mod+Shift+Right { spawn "sh" "-c" "niri msg action reset-window-height; niri msg action consume-or-expel-window-right"; }
    Mod+Shift+Down  { move-window-down-or-to-workspace-down; }
    Mod+Shift+Up    { move-window-up-or-to-workspace-up; }

    // ─── Resize ───
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+H     { set-column-width "-5%"; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+L     { set-column-width "+5%"; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+K     { set-window-height "-5%"; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+J     { set-window-height "+5%"; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+Left  { set-column-width "-5%"; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+Right { set-column-width "+5%"; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+Up    { set-window-height "-5%"; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+Down  { set-window-height "+5%"; }

    // Preset column widths (cycle through 1/3, 1/2, 2/3)
    Mod+R { switch-preset-column-width; }

    // ─── Workspaces (1-10) ───
    Mod+1 { focus-workspace 1; }
    Mod+2 { focus-workspace 2; }
    Mod+3 { focus-workspace 3; }
    Mod+4 { focus-workspace 4; }
    Mod+5 { focus-workspace 5; }
    Mod+6 { focus-workspace 6; }
    Mod+7 { focus-workspace 7; }
    Mod+8 { focus-workspace 8; }
    Mod+9 { focus-workspace 9; }
    Mod+0 { focus-workspace 10; }

    // Move window to workspace (follows, like Hyprland Ctrl+N)
    Mod+Ctrl+1 { move-column-to-workspace 1; }
    Mod+Ctrl+2 { move-column-to-workspace 2; }
    Mod+Ctrl+3 { move-column-to-workspace 3; }
    Mod+Ctrl+4 { move-column-to-workspace 4; }
    Mod+Ctrl+5 { move-column-to-workspace 5; }
    Mod+Ctrl+6 { move-column-to-workspace 6; }
    Mod+Ctrl+7 { move-column-to-workspace 7; }
    Mod+Ctrl+8 { move-column-to-workspace 8; }
    Mod+Ctrl+9 { move-column-to-workspace 9; }
    Mod+Ctrl+0 { move-column-to-workspace 10; }

    // Move window to workspace silently (like Hyprland Shift+N)
    Mod+Shift+1 { move-column-to-workspace 1; }
    Mod+Shift+2 { move-column-to-workspace 2; }
    Mod+Shift+3 { move-column-to-workspace 3; }
    Mod+Shift+4 { move-column-to-workspace 4; }
    Mod+Shift+5 { move-column-to-workspace 5; }
    Mod+Shift+6 { move-column-to-workspace 6; }
    Mod+Shift+7 { move-column-to-workspace 7; }
    Mod+Shift+8 { move-column-to-workspace 8; }
    Mod+Shift+9 { move-column-to-workspace 9; }
    Mod+Shift+0 { move-column-to-workspace 10; }

    // Scroll through workspaces (mouse wheel)
    Mod+WheelScrollDown cooldown-ms=150 { focus-workspace-down; }
    Mod+WheelScrollUp   cooldown-ms=150 { focus-workspace-up; }



    // ─── Volume Control ───
    XF86AudioRaiseVolume allow-when-locked=true { spawn "sh" "-c" "pactl set-sink-volume @DEFAULT_SINK@ +5%"; }
    XF86AudioLowerVolume allow-when-locked=true { spawn "sh" "-c" "pactl set-sink-volume @DEFAULT_SINK@ -5%"; }
    XF86AudioMute        allow-when-locked=true { spawn "sh" "-c" "amixer sset Master toggle"; }

    // ─── Playback Control ───
    XF86AudioPlay allow-when-locked=true { spawn "playerctl" "play-pause"; }
    XF86AudioNext allow-when-locked=true { spawn "playerctl" "next"; }
    XF86AudioPrev allow-when-locked=true { spawn "playerctl" "previous"; }

    // ─── Screen Brightness ───
    XF86MonBrightnessUp   { spawn "brightnessctl" "s" "+5%"; }
    XF86MonBrightnessDown { spawn "brightnessctl" "s" "5%-"; }

    // ─── Reload Config ───
    Mod+Shift+R { spawn "niri" "msg" "action" "load-config-file"; }

    // ─── Niri-Specific Extras ───
    // Toggle between column widths
    Mod+Minus         { set-column-width "-10%"; }
    Mod+Equal         { set-column-width "+10%"; }

    // Screenshot the whole screen
    Print { screenshot; }
    // Screenshot a specific window
    Ctrl+Print { screenshot-window; }
    // Screenshot a region
    Alt+Print { screenshot-screen; }

    // Move entire workspace between monitors
    Mod+Ctrl+Left  { move-workspace-to-monitor-left; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Right { move-workspace-to-monitor-right; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Up    { move-workspace-to-monitor-up; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Down  { move-workspace-to-monitor-down; }

    // Center the focused column
    Mod+C { center-column; }

    // Toggle between tiling and floating for window
    Mod+Slash { focus-workspace-previous; }

    // ─── Notifications (mako) ───
    Mod+Shift+D      { spawn "sh" "-c" "date >> /tmp/mako-bind.log; makoctl dismiss"; }
    Mod+Ctrl+Shift+D { spawn "makoctl" "dismiss" "--all"; }
    Mod+Shift+Comma  { spawn "makoctl" "restore"; }
    Mod+Shift+Period { spawn "makoctl" "menu" "rofi" "-dmenu" "-p" "Action"; }
}
